 {:id "adr-2607103000-kotoba-lang-standard-model-curvature-scalar-double-h-bug-fix"
  :title "ADR-2607103000: kotoba-lang/standard-model — curvature-scalar double-applied h; fixed by the independent review the previous landing ADR called for"
  :status "accepted"
  :date "2026-07-09"
  :deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"]
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kotoba-lang-standard-model"
  :authoritative true
  :authoritative_for
  ["follow-up to ADR-2607102700 (Phase 1 landing): acts on that ADR's own
    methodological note that independent review should follow any non-trivial
    GTG landing as standard practice, not an optional extra"
   "landed 2026-07-09: kotoba-lang/standard-model#11 merged as
    6296794a5eb5bec816e76994336685f453fc9012, 77 tests/2898 assertions, CI
    green (JDK17+21, after one transient infra retry -- 504 gateway timeout
    downloading Clojure CLI tooling, unrelated to code); superproject pin
    advanced via API single-entry commit 89edb0d773d9d40d089d2df2efcd6754b38c2e6b"
   "BUG: curvature-scalar computed gamma^a.(gamma^b.R(h_b^h_a)), contracting
    the ALREADY-COVARIANT riemann-basis-pair (eq 4.48, already built FROM h via
    L_a=a.hbar(grad)) against wedge(h_b,h_a) -- position-gauge-field ROWS --
    instead of fixed frame basis vectors e_a^e_b per eq (4.11)/(4.12). Since
    riemann-basis-pair already IS the covariant R (eq 4.9, R(B)=R(h(B)) for
    flat R + basis B), this applied h a SECOND time"
   "why CI-green Schwarzschild verification missed it: existing test checked
    only the SCALAR (trace). LDG's own Schwarzschild solution has
    h(e_1)=e_1,h(e_2)=e_2,h(e_3)=e_3 exactly (fixed points), so double-h is a
    no-op on purely-spatial pairs and only affects index-0 terms; the
    resulting genuinely-asymmetric ~1e-4-magnitude Ricci-TENSOR components
    (~2000x above the ~1e-10 FD-noise floor) happened to cancel in this
    solution's trace specifically -- independently reconfirmed by the
    requester (not just re-reading the reviewer's report) via a fresh REPL
    computation of the full tensor: buggy R_10~1.9e-4 vs R_01~9e-11
    (physically-impossible asymmetry, Ricci tensor must be symmetric) vs
    fixed formula uniformly ~1e-10 (correct)"
   "THIRD occurrence of this exact failure mode in this repo's GTG work (after
    PR #6 structure-constant slot order, and Phase 1's own first
    implementation attempt using the wrong covariant derivative) -- a
    seemingly-thorough single pass, confidently silently wrong, invisible to
    'tests pass', caught only by independent numeric verification against a
    ground truth STRONGER than the existing regression check"
   "FIX: riemann-basis-pair(b,a) called directly, no wedge-vectors/general
    riemann-map needed (both indices always fixed basis vectors here, never
    h-field rows). Argument order (b,a) vs (a,b) is explicitly disclosed in
    the docstring as ONLY algebraically justified (re-derived from eq
    4.11/4.12 structure), NOT independently numerically confirmed -- since
    riemann-basis-pair is antisymmetric and the only available verification
    (Schwarzschild) has R=0 identically, a sign error would be numerically
    invisible; honest caveat pending a literature worked example with a
    NONZERO known value or independent expert review of the derivation. The
    MAGNITUDE fix (the actual bug) IS independently numerically confirmed by
    two people from scratch; the sign convention is not"
   "added curvature-scalar-full-ricci-tensor-vanishes-not-merely-its-trace: a
    strictly stronger regression test checking every Ricci tensor component
    (not just trace) at both Schwarzschild points -- exactly the check that
    would have caught this bug at Phase 1's original landing"
   "scope check: frame-adjoint, H-field, omega-from-h, L-a-omega,
    riemann-basis-pair, riemann-map/riemann-map-matrix all independently
    RE-confirmed correct by the same review (multiple methods including a
    from-scratch Dirac-gamma-matrix verification path, kotoba.sm.spinor/gammas,
    fully independent of the FD-based riemann-map code path) -- bug isolated
    to curvature-scalar's final assembly step only"
   "methodological consequence: this is now the THIRD instance of this failure
    mode -- future GTG phases should treat independent adversarial review
    immediately after any non-trivial landing as standard operating procedure,
    and prefer regression tests checking the STRONGEST available invariant
    (here: full tensor) over the weakest convenient one (here: trace) when
    they are not provably equivalent under available test data -- they
    coincided here only because R=0 (vacuum) makes both vanish, a coincidence
    of the vacuum case not a general equivalence"
   "explicitly out of scope, unchanged: everything ADR-2607102300/2607102700
    already declared out of scope (matter coupling, Einstein multivector,
    GR-equivalence proof beyond Schwarzschild, quantization/RGE/scattering/
    lattice, dark-sector/de-Sitter) -- this ADR fixes a bug in already-in-scope
    code, does not widen scope"]
